  "evidence_limits": [
    "This is a 24-update numerical/performance smoke benchmark: 1 warmup plus 3 timed updates for each of 6 cases, not a convergence or full-training readiness result.",
    "All cases use a single step3750 checkpoint and the next four deterministic training batches. This avoids manually selecting fast samples but does not cover later trained states, independent seeds, or stiff/out-of-distribution trajectories.",
    "The six raw arrays were recorded BEFORE optimizer updates and reuse the same 32 training histories; shorter horizons are overlapping prefixes. They are not six independent validation sets, post-update rollout evidence, held-out tests, or 320-step rollouts.",
    "Final model/Adam tensors were deliberately not saved. Actual optimizer.step calls, finite nonzero gradients and 46 changed model tensors are supported by hash-bound executed source/runtime records; final Adam internal changes and final model hashes cannot be independently recalculated offline.",
    "The full training HDF5 is not present locally. Its hash is bound to the source checkpoint and runtime preflight; the four sampler index arrays are recorded and reused by verified code, but this audit did not re-read original pixels or regenerate the indices from the full dataset.",
    "Case order alternates by horizon and every measured update is included, but only three timings per case give no reliable confidence interval. Cache, clock and ordering effects remain possible.",
    "The algorithms implement different discrete maps and gradients. Their losses and timing must not be interpreted as an accuracy improvement or speed at matched numerical/prediction accuracy.",
    "No future-training stability, physical damping accuracy, general root uniqueness or full20k completion is established. No new training or rollout was run by this audit."
  ],
